          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em mapping cone
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
            in some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+category"} homotopical category
            (precisely: a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+cofibrant+objects"} category of cofibrant objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy cofiber
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p
            It is also called the
            %em
              homotopy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            or the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+quotient"} weak quotient
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            under
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p
            The dual notion is that of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cocone"} mapping cocone
          %p
            %img{:src => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/mappingcone.jpg", :width => "660"}/
          %p
            (graphics taken from
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Muro10"} Muro 2010
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            The mapping cone construction is a means to
            %em present
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
            the following canonical construction in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
          #InfinityCokernel.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              In an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pushout"} (∞,1)-pushout
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy cofiber
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pushout"} homotopy pushout
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi coker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Y
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi X
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    coker(f) \coloneqq Y \coprod_X {*}
            %p
              hence the object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+construction"} universally
              sitting in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ⇙
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi coker
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp; {*}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}} &amp;\swArrow_{\simeq}&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    Y &amp;\to&amp; coker(f)
                    }
                    \\,.
          #HomotopyCofiberByFactorizationLemma.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              If the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is presented by (is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} equivalent
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
              of) a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+cofibrant+objects"} category of cofibrant objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              (for instance given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+objects"} cofibrant objects
              in a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mn 1
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mi cyl
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi cone
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; X &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{i_1}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{i}}
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\stackrel{i_0}{\to}&amp; cyl(X)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; &amp;\searrow &amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    {*} &amp;\to&amp; &amp;\to&amp; cone(f)
                    }
            %p
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              using any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+object"} cylinder object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cyl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cyl(X)
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            This is discussed in detail at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+lemma"} factorization lemma
            and at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Intuitively this says that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cone(f)
              is the object obtained by
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  forming the cylinder over
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p
                  gluing to one end of that the object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                  as specified by the map
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %li
                %p shrinking the other end of the cylinder to the point.
            %p
              Intuitively it is clear that this way every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cycle"} cycle
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              that happens to be in the image of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              can be “continuously” translated in the cylinder-direction, keeping it constant in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              in the image of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              vanishes in the mapping cone. Hence in the mapping cone
              = succeed "." do
                %strong
                  the image of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  under
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                  is removed up to homotopy
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cone(f)
              is a homotopy-version of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo :
                    %mi cyl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta : cyl(X) \to Y
              out of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+object"} cylinder object
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo :
                    %mi g
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta : g \Rightarrow h
              between its restrictions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\coloneqq \eta(0)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \coloneqq \eta(1)
              to the cylinder boundaries
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi g
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi cyl
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi η
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi h
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{i_0}} &amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{g}}
                    \\\
                    cyl(X) &amp;\stackrel{\eta}{\to}&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \\uparrow^{\mathrlap{i_1}} &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{h}}
                    \\\
                    X
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Therefore prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyCofiberByFactorizationLemma"}
              says that the mapping cone is the the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal
              object with a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              and a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \circ f
              to the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+morphism"} zero morphism
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InfinityCokernel"}
              is saying.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The colimit in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyCofiberByFactorizationLemma"}
              may be computed in two stages by two consecutive
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushouts"} pushouts
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+diagram"} pasting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mi cyl
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi cyl
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi cone
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi cone
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; X &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{i_1} &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\stackrel{i_0}{\to}&amp; cyl(X) &amp;\to &amp; cyl(f)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    {*} &amp;\to&amp; cone(X) &amp;\to&amp; cone(f)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here every square is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
              is every rectangular pasting composite).
          %p
            This now is a basic fact in ordinary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
          #CylindersAndCones.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p The pushout
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mi cyl
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi cone
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\stackrel{i_0}{\to}&amp; cyl(X)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    {*} &amp;\to&amp; cone(X)
                    }
            %p
              defines the
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cone(X)
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (with respect to the chosen
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+object"} cylinder object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+object"} cylinder
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and identifying one
              = succeed "-shaped" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
            %p The pushout
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi cyl
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi cyl
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    cyl(X) &amp;\to&amp; cyl(f)
                    }
            %p
              defines the
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cylinder"} mapping cylinder
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cyl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cyl(f)
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              as the gluing map.
            %p The pushout
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi cyl
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi cyl
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi cone
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi cone
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    cyl(X) &amp;\to&amp; cyl(f)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    cone(X) &amp;\to&amp; cone(f)
                    }
            %p
              defines the
              %strong mapping cone
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cone(f)
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and then identifying one end with the point and the other with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p
            The geometric intuition behind this is best seen in the archetypical example of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
            %em
              %a{:href => "#ForTopologicalSpaces"} For topological spaces
            below. The example
            %em
              %a{:href => "InChainComplexes"} For chain complexes
            can be understood similarly geometrically by thinking of all chain complexes as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+chain+complex"} singular chains
            on topological spaces.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            We discuss realizations of the general construction in various contexts. Some of these examples are regarded in parts of the literature as the default examples, notably that
            %a{:href => "#ForTopologicalSpaces"} for topological spaces
            and that
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#InChainComplexes"} for chain complexes
          %h3#suspension Suspension
          %p
            The mapping cone of the morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to {*}
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+object"} suspension object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma X
            of an object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h3#ForTopologicalSpaces For topological spaces
          %p
            The notion
            %em mapping cone
            derives its name from its geometrical interpretation in the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
          %p
            For more details see also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+cofiber+sequence"} topological cofiber sequence
          %p
            With respect to the standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} model structure on topological spaces
            every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
            is a cofibrant object, and hence mapping cones on maps between CW-complexes have intrinsic meaning in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \coloneqq [0,1] \subset \mathbb{R} \in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+interval"} closed interval
            with its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+object"} interval object
            for the standard model structure. We may therefore take the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+object"} cylinder object
            of a topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to be
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cyl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi I
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  cyl(X) \coloneqq X \times I
                  \\,,
          %p
            which is literally the cylinder over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:X\to Y
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cone
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cone(f)
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cone
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi f
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  cone(f) =  (X \times I) \cup_{f} Y
          %p
            This is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times I
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            followed by an identification under which for each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
            a point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,1) \in X \times I
            is identified with the point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) \in Y
            and followed by the contraction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times \{0\}
            to a point.
          %p
            Of course the opposite convention is also possible: identify
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,0)
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x)
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and then contract
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times\{1\}
            to a point; the two constructions of cones are canonically homeomorphic; the first is sometimes called the “inverse mapping cone”.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+chain+complex"} singular chain complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
            sends the mapping cone to a mapping cone in the sense of chain complexes (up to conventions on the orientation of the interval and vector order in the definition of mapping cone of chain complexes).
          %h3#InChainComplexes For chain complexes
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo •
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet = Ch_\bullet(R Mod)
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
            for some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            (For instance if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = \mathbb{Z}
            the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet(Ab)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R Mod
            can be replaced by any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            in the following, with the evident changes in the presentation here and there.)
          %p
            We derive an explicit presentation of the mapping cone
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cone
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cone(f)
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+map"} chain map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CylindersAndCones"}
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ComponentsOfMappingConeInChainComplexes"}
            below, reproducing the classical formula for the mapping cone.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo *
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *_\bullet \in Ch_\bullet(\mathcal{A})
              for the chain complex concentrated on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              in degree 0
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo *
                      %mo •
                    %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    *_\bullet 0
                    \=
                    [\cdots \to 0 \to 0 \to R]
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              This may be understood as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normalized+chain+complex"} normalized chain complex
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homology"} chains of simplices
              on the terminal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^0
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
          #BoundaryInclusionIntoChainComplexIntervalObject.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_\bullet \in Ch_{\bullet}(\mathcal{A})
              be given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mo •
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi id
                        %mo ,
                        %mi id
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    I_\bullet
                    \=
                    (\cdots 0 \to 0 \to R \stackrel{(-id,id)}{\to} R \oplus R)
                    \\,.
            %p Denote by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mn 0
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mo *
                      %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i_0 : *_\bullet \to I_\bullet
            %p
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+map"} chain map
              which in degree 0 is the canonical inclusion into the second summand of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              and by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mo *
                      %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i_1 : *_\bullet \to I_\bullet
            %p correspondingly the canonical inclusion into the first summand.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              This is the standard
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+object+in+chain+complexes"} interval object in chain complexes
            %p
              It is in fact the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normalized+chain+complex"} normalized chain complex
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chains+on+a+simplicial+set"} chains on a simplicial set
              for the canonical simplicial interval, the 1-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"}> simplex
              \:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mo •
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    I_\bullet = C_\bullet(\Delta[1])
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi id
                    %mo ,
                    %mi id
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial^I = (-id, id)
              here expresses the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/alternating+face+map+complex"} alternating face map complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
              operator, which in terms of the three non-degenerate
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis"} basis
              elements is given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\partial ( 0 \to 1 ) = (1) - (0)
                    \\,.
          %p We decompose the proof of this statement is a sequence of substatements.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet \in Ch_\bullet
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (I \otimes X)_\bullet
                    \\in
                    Ch_\bullet
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+object"} cylinder object
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
              for the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+cofibrant+objects"} category of cofibrant objects
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet
              whose cofibrations are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
              and whose weak equivalences are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
              (the substructure of the standard
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} injective model structure on chain complexes
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              The complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (I \otimes X)_\bullet
              has components
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (I \otimes X)_n
                    \=
                    X_n \oplus X_n \oplus X_{n-1}
            %p
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
              is given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo ⊕
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mo ∂
                                  %mi X
                                %mo ⊕
                                %msup
                                  %mo ∂
                                  %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi n
                            %mo ⊕
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi n
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⊕
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mi id
                                %mo ,
                                %mi id
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⊕
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %msup
                                  %mo ∂
                                  %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X_{n+1} \oplus X_{n+1} &amp;\stackrel{\partial^X \oplus \partial^X}{\to}&amp; X_n \oplus X_n
                    \\\
                    \\oplus &amp;\nearrow_{(-id,id)}&amp; \oplus
                    \\\
                    X_{n} &amp;\underset{-\partial^X}{\to}&amp; X_{n-1}
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              hence in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+calculus"} matrix calculus
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi X
                              %mo ⊕
                              %msup
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi X
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mi id
                              %mo ,
                              %mi id
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %msup
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi X
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\partial^{I \otimes X}
                    \=
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    \\partial^X \oplus \partial^X &amp; (-id, id)
                    \\\
                    0 &amp; -\partial^X
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\;\;\colon\;\;
                    (X_{n+1} \oplus X_{n+1}) \oplus X_{n}
                    \\to
                    (X_{n} \oplus X_{n}) \oplus X_{n-1}
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By the formula discussed at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
              the components arise as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            .maruku-equation
